      },
      "prompts": [
        "What is the customer actually paying for?",
        "Which part of the business would be hardest to replace?",
        "What evidence would challenge the first impression?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Read the statements together",
      "paragraphs": [],
      "body": {
        "version": 1,
        "doc": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The income statement, balance sheet, and cash-flow statement offer different views of a business. Read them as a connected account rather than treating one headline number as the whole story."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A useful notebook separates the reported figure, the explanation offered for it, and the questions that remain. Differences between earnings and cash deserve investigation, not an automatic verdict."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "heading": "Write down what is still unknown",
      "paragraphs": [],
      "body": {
        "version": 1,
        "doc": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "End with an evidence list, not a confident target price. Record which claims are supported by filings, which rely on interpretation, and which require further work."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The finished research should make its limits as readable as its conclusions. That is the standard this sample format is designed to encourage."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
